# Conclusion
st.set_page_config(page_title="Data Quality Summary", layout="centered")

st.title("Text & Image Data Quality Summary")

st.header("✅ Conclusions")

with st.expander("Text Quality"):
    st.markdown("""
    - Null values in text were eliminated via concatenation → 0% nulls.
    - Redundant descriptions were resolved by keeping the longest version.
    - All product listings were unique (no unicity issues).
    - Preprocessing steps:
        - Removed HTML tags and stopwords
        - Cleaned residual HTML/JS
        - Translated to French
        - Applied lemmatization
    - Raw data was excluded due to noise from HTML artifacts.
    - Vectorization was optimized by grid search on:
        - Max token length
        - Min word frequency
        - Max vocabulary size
    """)

with st.expander("Image Quality"):
    st.markdown("""
    - Data augmentation and preprocessing were applied.
    - The model was kept simple as it performed sufficiently.
    - Overfitting occurred and was mainly due to parameter tuning.
    """)

st.header("Limitations")

st.markdown("""
- Source text data contained HTML and JS noise, requiring extra cleaning.
- Low-resolution images lacked zoom or proper focus on relevant product areas.
- Text printed on product boxes introduced confusion in image analysis.
- Free translation tools (e.g., Google Translate) gave poor performance.
""")

st.header("What We Would Do with More Time")

st.markdown("""
- Implement a smart zooming algorithm to center and enhance images.
- Blur or mask box text in images to avoid irrelevant visual noise.
- Use better translation tools or train a custom translation pipeline.
- Continue fine-tuning vectorization settings for optimal signal-to-noise.
- Avoid more complex models to reduce risk of overfitting.
""")
